﻿# Project Berunda

**AI-Native Crime Intelligence Platform for Karnataka State Police**

Document ID: BERUNDA-README | Version: 2.0 | Status: ACTIVE
Classification: PUBLIC | Owner: Berunda Team | Last Verified: 2026-07-18

---

## One-Line Value Proposition

Berunda transforms fragmented FIR records into a connected, queryable intelligence layer — geospatial hotspots, criminal link networks, and a grounded natural-language investigation assistant, built entirely on the mandatory Zoho Catalyst stack.

---

## Problem Statement

Karnataka's SCRB manages crime data in station-level Excel silos with no systematic link analysis, no proactive tooling, and fragmented visibility across districts. Investigators cannot:
- Cross-reference persons across multiple FIRs
- Detect emerging geographic crime patterns
- Query case data in natural language
- Receive explainable risk assessments

## Solution

A single platform where raw FIR data is ingested and normalized; analysts see spatiotemporal hotspots with temporal patterns; investigators see relationship graphs linking persons, locations, and vehicles across cases; and anyone can ask questions in plain English for grounded, cited answers.

---

## Core Features

| # | Capability | Status |
|---|------------|--------|
| 1 | Synthetic FIR import and entity extraction (English) | BUILDABLE |
| 2 | Cross-case person entity resolution with confidence scoring | BUILDABLE |
| 3 | Case/person relationship graph and hidden-link discovery | BUILDABLE |
| 4 | Geospatial hotspot map with district-to-station drill-down | BUILDABLE |
| 5 | Explainable risk scoring with feature-importance breakdown | BUILDABLE |
| 6 | Anomaly and spike detection against historical baselines | BUILDABLE |
| 7 | "Ask Berunda" grounded RAG over curated case corpus | BUILDABLE |
| 8 | Role-based authentication and authorization | BUILDABLE |
| 9 | Audit logging for sensitive reads and AI-assisted outputs | BUILDABLE |
| 10 | Live sensitive-feature exclusion and fairness verification | BUILDABLE |

