## Local Setup

### Prerequisites

- **Node.js** >= 20.0.0
- **Python** >= 3.11
- **PowerShell** 5.1+ (Windows) or **bash** (Linux/Mac)
- **Docker** and **Docker Compose** (optional, for containerized dev)
- **Catalyst CLI** (for Catalyst deployment)

### Quick Start

```powershell
# 1. Install dependencies
.\berunda.ps1 setup

# 2. Configure environment
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your settings

# 3. Run tests
.\berunda.ps1 test

# 4. Start development server
cd apps/web && npm run dev
```

### Docker Setup

```powershell
# Build and start all services
.\berunda.ps1 docker-build
.\berunda.ps1 docker-up
```

---

## Environment Variables

See `.env.example` for the complete list. Key variables:

| Variable | Description | Required |
|----------|-------------|----------|
| `APP_ENV` | Runtime environment | Yes |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Catalyst Data Store connection | Yes |
| `AUTH_SECRET` | JWT signing secret | Yes |
| `AI_API_KEY` | LLM provider API key | Yes |
| `CATALYST_ORG_ID` | Zoho Catalyst organization ID | Yes |
| `CATALYST_PROJECT_ID` | Zoho Catalyst project ID | Yes |

---

## Development Commands

```powershell
.\berunda.ps1 setup        # Install all dependencies
.\berunda.ps1 build        # Build all applications
.\berunda.ps1 test         # Run all tests
.\berunda.ps1 lint         # Run linters and type checkers
.\berunda.ps1 clean        # Remove build artifacts
.\berunda.ps1 docker-build # Build Docker images
```

## Testing Commands

```powershell
# Run all tests
pytest

# Unit tests only
pytest -m unit

# Integration tests only
pytest -m integration

# Frontend tests
cd apps/web && npm run test

# With coverage
pytest --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing
```

